# Roofline context-ladder rungs: the REPORT.md of each rung is committed; the
# 25-30 MB analytical.json per rung is regenerated deterministically by
# `make roofline` (about nine minutes) and is not committed.
results/roofline/context_ladder/*/*/analytical.json
# The speculative layer's two analytical.json files are 68 and 74 MB and are
# regenerated deterministically from the committed roofline artifacts by
# `make speculative`; only their REPORT.md is committed, as above.
results/roofline/speculative/*/analytical.json

# The operator-admission campaign's projection-matrix image: 8,388,608 BF16
# codes (42 MB per storage class) read from the pinned Qwen3-8B checkpoint at
# the shard, offset and SHA-256 the deployment's own object record declares.
# `tools/build_a3_operator_admission_vectors.py` re-derives it deterministically
# and the campaign byte-compares it on every run exactly as it does the
# committed images, so it is bound by content without being stored.
testdata/rtl/a3_operator_admission/weights.hex
testdata/rtl/a3_operator_admission_hbm/weights.hex

# Claude Code's per-session worktree metadata: tool state, not project content.
.claude/

# Routed-artifact convention (results/physical_abi3/*/*/pnr_artifacts/) keeps the
# whole ORFS bundle, netlists included, because for the small engines that bundle
# is ~1.8 MB. The microsequencer's is 107 MB -- 1_2_yosys.v is 60 MB and
# 6_final.v is 47 MB -- and Verilog netlists do not delta-compress, so storing
# them would permanently bloat the repository for evidence that config.mk plus
# the pinned sources already regenerate. The REPORTS are what the evidence cites
# (6_finish.rpt carries "max slew violation count 3204"; 5_route_drc.rpt is empty,
# i.e. zero routing DRC), so those stay tracked and only the netlists are ignored.
results/physical_abi3/asap7/a3_microsequencer/pnr_artifacts/1_2_yosys.v
results/physical_abi3/asap7/a3_microsequencer/pnr_artifacts/6_final.v
# Large netlists from the 2026-09-22/23 ASAP7 optimization runs, by the same rule as
# above: reports, config.mk and constraint.sdc are tracked; netlists over 5 MB are not.
results/physical_abi3/asap7/a3_attention_softmax_block/exp_only_cts12_1ns_artifacts/1_2_yosys.v
results/physical_abi3/asap7/a3_attention_softmax_block/exp_only_cts12_1ns_artifacts/6_final.v
